<script>
    var obj = {"start":0,"count":1,"name":"instagram-mobile","sport_id":null,"count_breakpoints":null,"css_class":"","pinned_id":"","extra":{},"context":null,"dummy":false,"type":"instagram","id":"956ed168-16ac-481d-9e15-d412d31649d1","data":[{"content_id":"18100492985454637","content_title":"The Bronx Community College (BCC) men's soccer team had three student-athletes recognized for their efforts during the 2026 campaign, as David Santa and Omar Sillah earned spots on the CUNY Community College All-Conference Team, while Santiago Vazquez was named to the All-Sportsmanship Team.\n\nSanta led the Broncos offensively throughout the season, finishing atop the squad in points, goals, and shots. The standout recorded 24 points and 11 goals while registering a team-high 40 shots. Santa also tied for the team lead in match-winning goals with two, showcasing his ability to deliver in crucial moments. His consistent production and offensive impact made him one of the Broncos' leading contributors in 2026, earning him well-deserved All-Conference recognition.\n\nSillah also made his mark on the Broncos' attack, finishing the season with seven points on three goals and one assist. His 16 shots ranked third on the team, highlighting his willingness to create scoring opportunities and contribute to the offensive effort. Sillah's production throughout the campaign earned him a place alongside Santa on the CUNY Community College All-Conference Team.\n\nMeanwhile, Vazquez was recognized for his sportsmanship and commitment to the values of collegiate athletics. Throughout the season, he consistently demonstrated a team-first mentality, treating coaches, teammates, and opponents with respect. His positive attitude and professionalism embodied the spirit of the game, making him a deserving selection to the CUNY Community College All-Sportsmanship Team.\n\nThe three selections highlight the contributions of the Broncos' student-athletes both on and off the field. Santa and Sillah's offensive production helped lead the way for Bronx Community College, while Vazquez's sportsmanship reflected the character and respect that the program strives to uphold.\n\nAll three of these young men played a pivotal role in helping the Broncos reach the NJCAA Region XV Tournament for the first time since 2022.\n\nCongratulations to David Santa, Omar Sillah, and Santiago Vazquez on their well-earned recognition!","content_date":"2026-10-27T09:21:18-05:00","content_url":"https://www.instagram.com/p/DfAD0JURn01/","content_image_url":"https://scontent-dfw5-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/870146658_18390473425227401_9090783510908270615_n.heic?stp=dst-jpg_e35_tt6&_nc_cat=102&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiRkVFRC5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=q322w_WxGHcQ7kNvwF_l47B&_nc_oc=Adqit_QEpMXnJi73zAITO_Ckn8n10L7x3Dux5JuUW4jBKhsa0zh4xUrn5wa7UzR-N2M&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-dfw5-2.cdninstagram.com&edm=AFF3FJ0EAAAA&_nc_gid=ils4CotxPKZRRaWxS-Fp8Q&_nc_ct=RQosPBUKFQIAAAA&oh=00_AQSsVUcAj8t1SmPm2IC0HwVa_9zrTmXfzrnnDYi4DxKKsg&oe=6B039094","link":"https://www.instagram.com/p/DfAD0JURn01/","id":"18100492985454637","tags":[],"comments":[],"likes":{"count":57},"images":{"thumbnail":null,"low_resolution":{"width":null,"height":null,"url":"https://scontent-dfw5-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/870146658_18390473425227401_9090783510908270615_n.heic?stp=dst-jpg_e35_tt6&_nc_cat=102&_nc_map=urlgen_bucketless&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiRkVFRC5iZXN0X2ltYWdlX3VybGdlbi5DMyJ9&_nc_ohc=q322w_WxGHcQ7kNvwF_l47B&_nc_oc=Adqit_QEpMXnJi73zAITO_Ckn8n10L7x3Dux5JuUW4jBKhsa0zh4xUrn5wa7UzR-N2M&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-dfw5-2.cdninstagram.com&edm=AFF3FJ0EAAAA&_nc_gid=ils4CotxPKZRRaWxS-Fp8Q&_nc_ct=RQosPBUKFQIAAAA&oh=00_AQSsVUcAj8t1SmPm2IC0HwVa_9zrTmXfzrnnDYi4DxKKsg&oe=6B039094"},"standard_resolution":{"width":null,"height":null,"url":"https://scontent-dfw5-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/870146658_18390473425227401_9090783510908270615_n.heic?stp=d